# Tap Web SDK

When the user wants to build a Tap app, read the `tap-getting-started` skill. After `install-skills.sh cursor`, it is at `.cursor/skills/tap-getting-started/SKILL.md`. In this repository it is at `plugins/tap-web-sdk/skills/tap-getting-started/SKILL.md`.

- Order: call `connect()` from a button click, then register callbacks, then enable input, then keep the page open. `connect()` starts notifications. There is no `start()`.
- `connect()` returns `TapSDKWeb` (v1) or `TapSDKWeb2` (v2). Handle both unless the user names the device. Check with `isTapSDKWeb2`.
- v1 needs `setInputMode(new InputModeController())` to get taps. v2 needs `setFeature(DeviceFeatures.MODEL_DETECTION, true)` plus a vision model.
- v1 tapcode is `number`. v2 tapcode is `number[]`. Use the first element on v2.
- Use Chrome, Edge, or Opera. The page must use HTTPS or localhost.
- Callbacks run on the Bluetooth path. Keep them short. Do not block.
- Knob and D-Pad recipes are v2 only (`tap-knob`, `tap-dpad`).
- Do not invent APIs or enum values. Test with the real device.
